      "role": "user",
      "content": "Got it, so it's about that controlled, calm vibe. But I'm wondering how we apply this universally in a global search. Some of our candidates come from very different cultural backgrounds—some might be much more expressive or high-energy, or have different ways of showing respect or authority in their native contexts. When we're looking for that \"universal\" executive presence for a top-tier global firm, are there certain cultural communication styles or social norms that just don't align with that \"commanding\" profile you're describing?",
